.TH STRUCTOR 1 "2026" "Livyatan Design Suite" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
structor \- CAD bench: solids in, drawings and cut files out
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B structor
.br
.B structor \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
Bare invocation opens the CAD window: drop primitive solids on the build
plate, drag/rotate/scale with gizmos, mark holes, group and boolean-merge,
then EXPORT STL or run SHOP EXPORT (cut files, flat patterns, dimensioned
sheets, and a BOM straight from the model). Press F on a part to cycle its
fabrication tag (FLAT/ROLLED/CNC/PRINT/CAST/STOCK); Shift+F steps a ROLLED
part's seam, Shift+T its plate gauge.
.PP
SAVE (Ctrl+S) and OPEN (Ctrl+O) keep the scene as a .SigN file (readable
JSON-CSG) through the file dialog, default folder ~/Structor; the scene also
autosaves to ~/Structor/autosave.SigN once a minute when it changed. HIDE
takes the selected parts out of the viewport, SHOW ALL restores them; hidden
parts still export. The inspector's Z row is the part's base: Z = 0 rests it
on the plate. The parts list under the palette hides/shows (dot) and selects
(name). REST drops the selection onto the plate (or onto the other picked
part); FIT ALL (H, nothing selected) frames every part; MEASURE reads the
distance between two clicked points; RECENT reopens one of the last five
scenes; UNDO/REDO carry their depth; UNITS switches the inspector and
readouts between mm and inches; Ctrl+I imports, Ctrl+E exports STL. A
palette click leaves the keyboard in the new part's first dimension field.
New parts arrive at 25.4 mm. Hover a toolbar button for its chord. A+ / A-
scale the UI text of every Livyatan module (restart to apply).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SIG_OPEN
Path to a .SigN scene to load at launch.
.TP
.B SIG_IMPORT
STL/OBJ to import at launch.
.TP
.B SIG_UNITS
Set to
.B in
to start the UNITS toggle in inches (default mm).
.TP
.B SIG_COOP_W
Initial DEBUG pane width in pixels (default 340; dragging clamps to 240\-720).
.TP
.B SIG_BG_LIFT
Backdrop lift = the Y of the backdrop placement (see SIG_BG_X/Z/YAW/PITCH/ROLL).
The placement the operator locks (MAGIC CARPET in the DEBUG pane, or VIEW > BG
LEVEL) lives in ~/.config/structor/backdrop.json and overrides these defaults.
.TP
.B SIG_BG_X, SIG_BG_Z, SIG_BG_YAW, SIG_BG_PITCH, SIG_BG_ROLL
Launch defaults for the backdrop placement around the plate (world units, degrees).
.TP
.B SIG_SSAO
Set to
.B 1
to enable SSAO (off by default: it bands the skydome).
.TP
.B SIG_INPUT_TRACE
Set (any value) to print WHEEL/PAN input events to stderr.
.TP
.B STRUCTOR_ICON_OUT
Test-only: directory the ignored test dump_palette_shapes writes the palette
shape STLs to (the source of the palette icons). Does nothing in the binary.
.TP
.B SIG_VIEW
Test-only: "yaw,pitch,radius" poses the camera at launch for headless shots.
.TP
.B DROP_QA
In-process QA script path (the drop toolkit's lane); unset in normal use.
.TP
.B LIVYATAN_THEME
Palette for comparison shots (livyatan, tokyo-night, gruvbox, catppuccin);
the default is what ships.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/Structor/
Default folder for SAVE / OPEN and the once-a-minute autosave.SigN.
.PP
The full env-knob table (mouse/puck feel, per-axis sign trims, backdrop
orientation) is in the MANUAL; the NAV panel and nav.json are the durable home
for feel.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/structor/nav.json
Navigation feel (every sign/source/sensitivity; edited live in the NAV panel).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR hephaestus (1),
.BR labyrinth (1),
.BR livyatan (7).
Full manual: /usr/share/doc/structor/MANUAL.md
